"""Separate project-board styling from reference-led generation."""
def style_instructions(project_name):
 return f'''PROJECT STYLE ADAPTATION — this operation supersedes earlier reference-style instructions.
The previous production is the CONTENT source, never the style authority. Match {project_name}'s own presentation boards and job AGENTS.md. Do not preserve the old Pinterest/reference palette or import another project's conventions.
Open the previous production and the supplied project board previews. Read project rules. Write reference_analysis.md identifying the actual board sources, observed palette by semantic role, typography, line weights, texture and annotation conventions. Explicit written project rules override conflicting historical board styling. If visual board evidence is unavailable, use the written rules and record this limitation; never invent an established style.
Keep the production's geographic extent, orientation, real geometry, meaningful content, composition and verified dimensions. Do not regenerate a generic basemap, crop to the default site boundary, move features, flatten detail, or paste the drawing onto a board. Adjust only styling and necessary label spacing. Preserve factual labels while translating any non-English text.
Map colours semantically (vegetation, water, context, materials), not through a global tint/filter. Match project typography at actual print sizes, linework, dash patterns, leaders and architectural entourage. Keep dark detail legible and restrained context visible. Apply special water colours only where the project's rules specify them. Never add decorative frames, filler text or fabricated facts.
Produce a standalone board-ready drawing with the same composition and output dimensions; preserve editability where source geometry permits. Export matching high-resolution PNG and PDF plus genuinely editable SVG when feasible; do not call an embedded raster editable. Keep existing print scales only when geometrically valid.
Render and OPEN the result beside both the previous production and the target project boards at sheet and detail scale. Compare content/geometry preservation against the previous production, and palette/linework/typography against the project boards and rules. Correct deficiencies before delivery.
Write style_review.json in the job root using the v4 contract above. In that contract, reference means the TARGET PROJECT BOARD STYLE, not the original inspiration. Include all required composition, visual_hierarchy, context_density, linework_palette, target_geometry and render_inspected checks, actual visual observations and limitations. Composition/content should remain consistent with the previous production; evaluate linework and palette against the project style. Mark failed checks honestly.
'''
